['To create a simple web application that accepts a PDF file, you'll need a server-side framework like Flask or Django and a client-side technology like HTML/CSS/JavaScript (Frontend) and Python (Backend). Here's an example of how you can achieve this using Flask for the backend and HTML/CSS/jQuery for the frontend.

First, let's set up the backend with Flask:

```python
from flask import Flask, request, send_from_directory, make_response, render_template
import os

app = Flask(__name__)
upload_folder = 'uploads'

if not os.path.exists(upload_folder):
    os.makedirs(upload_folder)

@app.route('/', methods=['GET'])
def index():
    return render_template('index.html')

@app.route('/upload', methods=['POST'])
def upload():
    file = request.files['file']
    if file.filename.endswith('.pdf'):
        filepath = os.path.join(upload_folder, file.filename)
        file.save(filepath)
        return make_response('File uploaded successfully!', 200)
    else:
        return make_response('Invalid file type. Please upload a PDF file.', 400)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

Next, let's create the frontend for uploading the PDF file using HTML/CSS/jQuery:

Create a folder called `templates`, inside this folder create an `index.html` file and paste the following code:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>PDF Uploader</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Upload PDF File</h1>
    <form id="uploadForm" action="/upload" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
        <input type="file" name="file" accept=".pdf">
        <button type="submit">Upload</button>
    </form>
    <div id="message"></div>
    <script src="/static/script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Create a `static` folder, inside this folder create two files: `style.css` and `script.js`.

Add some basic styling to style.css, such as:

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}
form {
    width: 300px;
    margin: auto;
    text-align: center;
}
button {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
}
#message {
    color: green;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 20px;
}
```

In script.js, add the following code to handle the upload response and display a success message when the file is uploaded successfully:

```javascript
$(document).ready(function() {
    $("#uploadForm").on("submit", function(e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        $.ajax({
            url: $(this).attr('action'),
            type: 'POST',
            data: new FormData(this),
            contentType: false,
            processData: false,
            success: function(data) {
                $("#message").html(data);
            },
            error: function() {
                $("#message").html("Error while uploading the file.");
            }
        });
    });
});
```

This code uses jQuery to submit the form using AJAX, handle the success and error responses, and display a message on the screen. With this setup, you can run the Flask server and access the web app at `http://localhost:5000/`. Users will be able to upload PDF files, which are saved in the 'uploads' folder.']

